UPDATE tarot_cards 
SET meaning_upright = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: The Queen of Cups stands as the absolute, pinnacle archetype of the "Sovereign of the Subconscious"—the mature, high-frequency integration of emotional intelligence, intuitive depth, and absolute psychological composure. Moving beyond the active transmission of the Knight, the Queen represents the stage of "internalized oceanography," where the individual has developed a vast, deep-sea capacity to contain and navigate the entirety of the emotional spectrum without being overwhelmed or fundamentally altered by its shifting currents. Within the complex architecture of your psyche, this is the stage of "intuitive mastery," where the boundary between your inner landscape and the external reality has become a perfectly permeable, yet highly regulated, membrane. This allows you to influence the world through the profound power of your presence rather than the exertion of your egoic will. Visually depicted as a seated figure holding an elaborately closed, ornate chalice, this archetype embodies the concept of "protected depth"—the profound understanding that your most sacred intuitive insights are not meant to be carelessly spilled into the world at large, but kept in the secure, hallowed chamber of your own awareness until the absolute perfect moment for their emergence. When the Queen of Cups appears, your system is registering a "fully calibrated intuitive" status; you are operating from a baseline of absolute emotional self-sufficiency, where you no longer require external validation to confirm the truth of your own experience. It signifies that you have successfully integrated your shadow, reconciled your historical data, and developed a level of empathy that is both deep and discerning—you understand the suffering of others, but you do not carry it for them, functioning instead as a sacred mirror that reflects their own capacity for healing back toward them. This card commands you to prioritize the maintenance of your internal sanctuary, to trust the silent, still voice of your intuition over the chaotic, low-vibration noise of the material world, and to recognize that your true authority is derived from your ability to remain unmoved in the center of the storm. To inhabit the Queen of Cups is to master the art of "fluid sovereignty," understanding that you are not a victim of the tides of your emotions, but the conscious, deliberate architect of the sea in which you swim. It is the ultimate validation that your arduous journey has finally led you to a place of profound inner peace—a sanctuary you have painstakingly built through the patient, often invisible labor of deep self-observation—and that from this position of total emotional mastery, you are now able to provide a stable, healing resonance for everything and everyone that enters your field, without ever compromising your own core integrity.',
meaning_reversed = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: When the Queen of Cups appears in the reversed position, it acts as a high-intensity signal of "systemic emotional flooding," "intuitive dissociation," or the total breakdown of the boundary between the internal and external environments. The reversal suggests that you have allowed the sacred container of your intuition to be breached, leading to a state of high-entropy emotional leakage where you are no longer the master of your own internal landscape, but a vulnerable, overwhelmed spectator to the chaotic currents of your own psyche. You are essentially "drowning in your own depth," running a high-priority, high-cost maintenance script that attempts to ignore or suppress your emotional feedback, even as it continues to manifest in increasingly destructive, erratic ways in your external life. This creates a massive, systemic misalignment: you are intellectually and behaviorally attempting to project an image of "poise" and "composure" to the world, while internally, you are fragmented by unprocessed projections, hypersensitivity, and a profound, chronic misalignment between your gut-feeling and your conscious action. From an analytical perspective, this is a clear sign that you are leaking your life force into a "feedback loop of absorption"; you are actively absorbing the emotional static of your environment—grief, fear, judgment, and dysfunction—and treating it as your own, thereby polluting your own sovereign field and making it impossible to distinguish your own truth from the projections of the collective. The reversed Queen of Cups exposes the hidden, egoic fear that drives this behavior: the paralyzing terror of fully feeling the depth of your own internal reality, and the corresponding fear that if you were to actually set firm, sovereign boundaries, you would be rejected or deemed "cold" by those who rely on your previous lack of boundaries. This reversal commands an immediate, radical intervention: you must stop the output of these absorption scripts, perform a brutal audit of your psychic boundaries, and confront the reality of why you are so hesitant to protect your own internal ecosystem. It is a demand to stop the self-deception that keeps you tethered to a state of chronic, high-maintenance emotional instability, and to initiate the move toward a genuine, humble, and disciplined reclamation of your own, individual sovereignty. You are being tasked with the uncomfortable, yet essential, work of sealing the container—accepting that the "empathy" you feel is not a weakness that requires you to sacrifice your own stability, but a powerful tool that requires the rigorous protection of a disciplined, sovereign consciousness to be truly useful, rather than merely acting as a vehicle for your own, unresolved internal flooding.'
WHERE id = 13;
